    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the July 1st slate with **Junior Caminero** (84.17) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) headlining the lineup as our most efficient starts. **Junior Caminero** benefits from a high-upside matchup against Lugo, compounded by favorable wind conditions and a solid xwOBA, while **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is maximized by his leadoff spot and a significant dynamic platoon advantage against Buehler. While **Yordan Alvarez** (73.65) and **Lars Nootbaar** (65.69) provide stable production, we are keeping a close eye on **Casey Schmitt** (63.20); his score assumes a #3 spot in the lineup, where his ability to exploit a high xERA from Gallen\u2014combined with the potential for stolen bases against a slower-delivering starter\u2014makes him a sneaky pivot into the upper tier of today's starters.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved the final utility slot. **Caleb Durbin** (46.50) earned the start based on his baseline projections, but he faced stiff competition from **Chase Meidroth** (43.96) and **Jacob Gonzalez** (43.55). Ultimately, **Caleb Durbin** was selected due to his favorable park factor, though he carries risk against a stingy opposing pitcher and an elite defensive catcher. We are exercising caution with **Trea Turner** (54.45) and **Kyle Schwarber** (53.07); both are seeing their raw numbers suppressed by a difficult matchup against Skenes, further hampered by the opposing catcher's elite pop time. While their pedigree keeps them in the lineup, their efficiency is undeniably constrained by the Skenes encounter. We continue to monitor the status of **Christian Yelich** and **Rece Hinds**, who remain unavailable as we look to maximize our daily game caps with active, high-efficiency matchups.",
